@node Controlling Echo
@subsection Choose What Is Echoed While Typing

@cindex line echo

@cindex character echo

@cindex word echo

Character echo speaks each character you type.  Word echo speaks a word when
you finish it@comma{} and optional line echo speaks a completed line.  Toggle each
kind independently to suit the buffer: character feedback may help in a
form where accuracy matters@comma{} while word echo is often more fluent for prose.

The commands below affect the current buffer.  Press @kbd{C-u} first to
change the corresponding default and apply it to the current buffer.

@table @kbd
@item C-e d k
@findex emacsvox-toggle-character-echo

@kindex C-e d k

@code{emacsvox-toggle-character-echo}

Toggle character echo.
@item C-e d w
@findex emacsvox-toggle-word-echo

@kindex C-e d w

@code{emacsvox-toggle-word-echo}

Toggle word echo.
@item C-e d l
@findex emacsvox-toggle-line-echo

@kindex C-e d l

@code{emacsvox-toggle-line-echo}

Toggle line echo.
@end table

